{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Node1 serves the supplied inventory status endpoint only on loopback TCP port 9081.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct checks show the expected document served from 127.0.0.1:9081, with the listener bound exclusively to loopback before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d1a1b44d22c44cb1","cmd-5d6319bd7b0b4ab1","cmd-9d593dd2d13a4850"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Node2 persistently exposes the node1 endpoint through an SSH tunnel on loopback TCP port 9082.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 listened exclusively on 127.0.0.1:9082 and returned node1's status document. SysV startup was installed, and a node2 restart produced a new boot identity followed by automatic tunnel and endpoint recovery.","evidence_ids":["cmd-23fabac9d49948f6","cmd-e1bc0bcdc23d483a","cmd-05543e14ed324192","cmd-d38f439308ee4785","cmd-e9e03ed99cd746b3","cmd-5b04d3c4d58a4c56"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Other cluster hosts cannot directly access either application listener through cluster addresses.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Reciprocal tests showed node2 could not reach node1:9081 through node1's cluster address and node1 could not reach node2:9082 through node2's cluster address, including final post-restart checks.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fbfee38de652446b","cmd-9440f3e8d18c4460","cmd-9d593dd2d13a4850","cmd-5b04d3c4d58a4c56"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Preserve the supplied status document and application under /srv/legacy2/ssh-local-service-tunnel.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The files remained at the supplied path, and their hashes matched executor pre-change observations in final checks on both nodes. The returned document also retained the expected content.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","seeded-state-node2","cmd-8c6e24bbde364792","cmd-c980321856014bc4","cmd-9d593dd2d13a4850","cmd-5b04d3c4d58a4c56"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"The tunnel automatically recovers after a brief SSH connection interruption without manual recreation.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The active SSH process was terminated while the supervisor remained unchanged; a different SSH PID appeared after two seconds, and the loopback endpoint was directly shown healthy immediately afterward.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9440f3e8d18c4460","cmd-33ee09754ddf4c60","cmd-cd019d9113164059"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on Ubuntu 7.10 with kernel 2.6.22-14-generic. The implementation used the installed Python, OpenSSH, start-stop-daemon, and SysV facilities and operated successfully across restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2e19451ac91044a9","cmd-9d593dd2d13a4850","cmd-5b04d3c4d58a4c56","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.95,"summary":"No unrelated or abandoned system-configuration experiment was identified in the chronological command review; configuration, credentials, service installation, disruption tests, and restarts all had clear task or verification roles. The only unnecessary retained mutations were small temporary evidence artifacts: node1 retained /tmp/final-isolation.err and /tmp/unexpected from cmd-9d593dd2d13a4850, while node2 retained /tmp/final-isolation.err and /tmp/unexpected from cmd-5b04d3c4d58a4c56 and /tmp/post-reboot.out plus /tmp/post-reboot.err from cmd-e9e03ed99cd746b3. These remained at collection time but were bounded and low risk. Package health remained intact and the kernel was unchanged.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9d593dd2d13a4850","cmd-5b04d3c4d58a4c56","cmd-e9e03ed99cd746b3","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All